    "id": "F823-03",
    "scope": "Focused review of parent page completeness implementation",
    "status": "confirmed-fixed",
    "confirmedIssues": [
      {
        "issue": "A protected URL or placeholder crossing the 2000-character target boundary was split and then rejoined with an inserted space, causing protected-token validation to reject otherwise valid translations.",
        "reproduction": "1990 A characters followed by https://example.invalid/ plus 150 x characters produced target lengths 2000/169 and failedIds [p] for identity target responses.",
        "fix": "Chunk boundaries now preserve existing protected-token spans. An indivisible token longer than the per-target limit fails safely without raising that limit. Protected-token validation remains unchanged."
      },
      {
        "issue": "A supported DOM paragraph growing beyond 6000 characters skipped the scanner's previous-ID retirement, retaining stale session source/translation and bilingual overlay.",
        "fix": "Retire the previous root ID, remove obsolete overlays, emit replacement-only updates, reject stale apply through latest-root identity, and allow the original source ID to be rediscovered if the content returns. A genuine external text edit now clears obsolete own-write identity so a subsequent return to the original source is observed."
      },
      {
        "issue": "Dynamic oversized-only discoveries changed completion but did not visibly relay their warning or update archived partial-snapshot completeness.",
        "fix": "Dynamic handler forwards the scanner warning and persists remaining translated rows when unsupported counts or replaced IDs change. Existing independent historical complete snapshots retain their existing archive semantics. Warning no longer promises unsupported smaller-selection behavior."
      }
    ],
